  See also `tf.size`, `tf.rank`.

  `tf.shape` returns a 1-D integer tensor representing the shape of `input`.
  For a scalar input, the tensor returned has a shape of (0,) and its value is
  the empty vector (i.e. []).

  For example:

  >>> tf.shape(1.)
